{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1347103-conservation-of-psi-energy","id":1347103,"title":"Conservation of (Psi) Energy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-08T14:41:07-08:00","id":1347103,"title":"Conservation of (Psi) Energy","content":"So you get my buy in that Psi powers loop around the Conservation of Energy by pulling from an invisible field, but can that invisible field be exhausted, even if temporarily? Obviously the Psi available for a given user runs out, but then they refill that tank so to speak, but can there be so much Psi activity that it drains the available noetic juice from an area?<br /> <br /> I guess it could also be explained that the new energy and or matter seemingly created out of psi could bleed back into the noetic background over time: the system eventually returning to equilibrium.<br /> <br /> Would you welcome the idea of Psi dead zones into your game, as a player or SG? Not just the increased difficulty and cost of the QFZs (although I could see similar rules being used), but your characters don't regen Psi points at all in the area?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T15:38:14-08:00","id":1347114,"title":"","content":"I would be okay with Psi dead zones if they are very rare, very hard to create, and very important to whatever the plot of the campaign is. I would also be fine with it if the absence of Psi energy leads to all sorts of other troubles - like life itself is near to zero in such a place and even the environment is dead. <br /> <br /> On the whole could Psi energy be exhausted, my answer to that would be no. It is a limitless energy. It is never destroyed, it just transforms between forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T17:03:40-08:00","id":1347135,"title":"","content":"In a normal area no number of psi-capable humans using their powers will drain it. You can have low and dead-psi areas - usually where plenty of corruption energies force the psi out. <br /> <br /> As a SG, you can introduce low-psi areas that can be exhausted, or that reduce psi recharge, as easily as you like. I\u2019m certainly onboard with low psi planets/areas being out there as mysteries and challenges for characters to overcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T09:03:25-08:00","id":1347253,"title":"","content":"In a normal area of space, there's no way to exhaust psi, any more than you can &quot;use up&quot; the gravity. The universe's ambient psi will rush to fill in any gaps faster than you can make it. Even if everyone on Earth were psi-active and using their powers at once, it's unlikely they'd notice any interruption in flow.<br /> <br /> Of course, quantum energies may make it more difficult to access psi, so some QFZs may effectively be noetically dead. It may theoretically be possible to put up &quot;walls&quot; so that no new psi rushes to fill a gap, and thus a psion may exhaust all the psi in an area, but so far no one's managed it.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that other races might have put together massive planet-sized psi engines for unknown purposes, which use psi so quickly that they're effectively &quot;black holes&quot; for psi, with nearby psions unable to use any before it rushes out of their grasp. It'd be a danger to any jumpships that stray too near, since they may be unable to gather enough psi to escape.<br /> <br /> Humans are easily centuries away from that kind of technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}